1. Install CMake
Go to https://cmake.org/ and download CMake. Install Cmake with instructions.
STEPS use CMake 3.28 or newer version. Older version may work, however, it is not tested.

2. Install gcc and g++
2.1 Windows
On Windows, go to https://www.mingw-w64.org/ and download pre-built MinGW.
You can find MinGW-W64-builds on https://github.com/niXman/mingw-builds-binaries/releases.
Download version with "poxis-seh" (such as posix-seh-ucrt-rt).
Unpack the downloaded version to any directory you like.

2.2 Linux
On linux, you can install gcc with command. For example, on Debian or Ubuntu, you can try:
sudo apt install gcc g++

2.3 Check version
Make sure you have the latest version of gcc and g++.
You can check the version with following command:
gcc --version
g++ --version

3. Build STEPS
3.1 Go to build directory
If there is no build directory like "steps/build", create one.
Then cd to build directory with command:
cd steps/build
3.2 Generate Makefile
In steps/build directory, run following command to generate Makefile:
cmake -G "MinGW Makefiles" ..    # for Windows
or
cmake -G "Unix Makefiles" ..     # for Linux
If you can not find gcc or g++ on Window, you may need to check the Compiler variable in the CMakeLists.txt.

3.3 Build STEPS
Run the following command to build STEPS:
make  # for Linux
or
"D:\Program Files\mingw-64\x86_64-15.1.0-posix-seh-ucrt-rt_v12-rev0\bin\mingw32-make.exe"   # for Windows
If you want to speed up compilation, you can add -j option to make command.
For example,
make -j4  # for Linux
or
"D:\Program Files\mingw-64\x86_64-15.1.0-posix-seh-ucrt-rt_v12-rev0\bin\mingw32-make.exe" -j4  # for Windows




